@startuml act-backup
!include _style.iuml
title Automatic backups: BackupScheduler.TickAsync (every 30 s) and BackupService.CreateAsync

|BackupScheduler|
start
if (first tick?) then (yes)
  :remember the newest valid backup per tier;\ndelete stale *.partial files;
endif
:StorageService.WriteCount changed?\n-> pending since now (restarts the 2 minutes);
if (pending for 2 min?) then (yes)
  :create Recent (skip if same as newest Recent);
endif
if (last 2-hourly >= 2 h ago?) then (yes)
  :create TwoHourly (skip if same as newest);
endif
if (no Daily today and (startup or changed today)?) then (yes)
  :create Daily (always written);
endif
|BackupService|
:wait until no write for 2 s (give up after 30 s: NotQuiet);
if (data.ttmdata exists?) then (no)
  :NothingToBackUp;
  stop
endif
:read data, settings, sync settings (shared read)\nand check each parses -> else SourceUnreadable;
:read every linked sync file\n(missing or broken: listed with Included = false);
if (automatic tier, no templates and no sync sources?) then (yes)
  :NothingToBackUp\n(an empty state would push real backups out);
  stop
endif
if (fingerprint equals the newest of the tier?) then (yes)
  :Unchanged;
  stop
endif
:write ttm-backup-<tier>-<time>.zip.partial\n(files, then manifest.json with sizes + SHA-256), flush;
:Verify: re-open, every hash and parse checked;
if (valid?) then (yes)
  :rename to .zip -> Created;
  |BackupScheduler|
  :Prune(tier): keep newest valid 3 / 5 / 5\n(damaged ones neither count nor get deleted);
else (no)
  |BackupService|
  :delete .partial -> Failed (tried again next tick);
endif
stop
@enduml
